ir, post-generation recovery, and pull-request\\n./forge/docs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:578:persistent-instruction state, Gradle command output, metadata-fix output,\\n./forge/docs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:579:native tracing output, post-generation intervention output, and local\\n./forge/docs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:695:| `SUCCESS_WITH_INTERVENTION_STATUS` | Tests succeeded after the built-in post-generation recovery modified the working tree (an analysis-agent metadata repair, then the same role removing unsupported failing tests as a last resort), and the local CI-equivalent verification (§FS-local-ci-equivalent-verification) passed. The intervention's record is included in the run-metrics and PR description, and is written to the run's durable logs rather than into the tree Forge publishes, so a recovered run carries no Forge run artifact into its pull request and cannot be classified as a repository-level change by that artifact alone (§FS-human-intervention-policy). PR-eligible; distinct from the `human-intervention` label unless §FS-human-intervention-policy separately requires that label. |\\n./forge/docs/functional-spec/publication.md:296:must not depend on any workflow implementation or on the post-generation\\n./forge/docs/functional-spec/benchmarking.md:56:  starting/ending commit, and post-generation intervention details when used\\n./forge/docs/architecture/git-scripts.md:87:  post-generation intervention, and Forge revision evidence;\\n./forge/docs/architecture/git-scripts.md:209:any post-generation intervention, and local verification commands and outcomes\\n./forge/docs/architecture/drivers.md:189:deterministic post-generation merge.\\n./forge/docs/architecture/agent.md:87:select recovery, style, native-test, post-generation, and review work; the\\n./forge/docs/architecture/architecture.md:19:| §AR-forge-strategy-agent-boundary | how strategy configuration, workflow engines, agents, and post-generation interventions are