st-generation-fix\\\", f\\\"{backend} post-generation fix completed for {coordinates}\\\")\\n./forge/ai_workflows/core/metadata_fix.py:33:    fallback_log_path = build_task_log_path(\\\"metadata-fix\\\", coordinates, \\\"metadata-fix.log\\\")\\n./forge/ai_workflows/core/metadata_fix.py:61:        developer_instructions += f\\\"\\\\n\\\\nLocal metadata-fix procedure:\\\\n{skill_file.read()}\\\"\\n./forge/ai_workflows/core/metadata_fix.py:81:        task_type=\\\"metadata-fix\\\",\\n./forge/ai_workflows/core/metadata_fix.py:127:        \\\"Hard requirement for this metadata-fix run: every Gradle, Java, and native-image command \\\"\\n./forge/ai_workflows/core/workflow_strategy.py:338:        \\\"\\\"\\\"Run Gradle tests for a library and classify post-generation failures.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n./forge/ai_workflows/core/workflow_strategy.py:361:            log_detail(\\\"post-generation-test\\\", f\\\"Running {stage_name} for {library}\\\")\\n./forge/ai_workflows/core/workflow_strategy.py:370:                log_detail(\\\"post-generation-test\\\", f\\\"{stage_name} passed for {library}\\\")\\n./forge/ai_workflows/core/workflow_strategy.py:378:            # Repairing a failed post-generation lane is the finalization phase's\\n./forge/ai_workflows/core/workflow_strategy.py:386:                log_detail(\\\"metadata-fix\\\", f\\\"Running metadata fix workflow for {library} after {stage_name} failure\\\")\\n./forge/ai_workflows/core/workflow_strategy.py:405:                            \\\"post-generation-test\\\",\\n./forge/ai_workflows/core/workflow_strategy.py:416:                    \\\"post-generation-fix\\\",\\n./forge/ai_workflows/core/workflow_strategy.py:425:                        \\\"post-generation-timeout-seconds\\\",\\n./forge/ai_workflows/core/workflow_strategy.py:429:                        \\\"post-generation-test-output-chars\\\",\\n./stats/io.netty/netty-codec/4.2.2.Final/forge-publication.json:98:    \\\"analysis_markdown\\\": \\\"# Post-generation intervention\\\\n\\\\nLibrary: io.netty:netty-codec:4.2.2.Final\\\\n\\\\nStage: `metadata_fix_failed`\\\\n\\\\n## Failure summary\\\\n\\\\nThe native test suite had one failure: `ByteBufChecksumInnerReflectiveByteBufChecksumTest.gzipDecoderUpdatesChecksumFromDirectInputBuffer()`. The reported `IllegalReferenceCountException` occurred during `EmbeddedChannel` cleanup after Netty's direct-buffer cleaner path had already failed.\\\\n\\\\n## Root cause and action\\\\n\\\\nThe metadata-fix log identified the underlying failure as an `UnsupportedFeatureError`: Netty 4.2.2 selects `CleanerJava24` on Java 24+, and that cleaner calls `Arena.ofShared`, while this Native Image was built without `-H:+SharedArenaSupport`. This is an unsupported Native Image platform feature, not missing reachability metadata. Enabling it requires a hosted Native Image option that cannot be supplied by `reachability-metadata.json` and must not be shipped as a metadata-side runtime change. §root/FS-repository-functional-spec.3\\\\n\\\\nRemoved the generated test file:\\\\n\\\\n- `tests/src/io.netty/netty-codec/4.1.42.Final/src/test/java/io_netty/netty_codec/ByteBufChecksumInnerReflectiveByteBufChecksumTest.java`\\\\n\\\\nThe pre-existing metadata diff was left untouched, and no test-only support file was exclusive to the removed test.\\\\n\\\\n## Verification\\\\n\\\\n`./gradlew test -Pcoordinates=io.netty:netty-codec:4.2.2.Final --stacktrace` passed after removal: all eight remaining native tests succeeded.\\\\n\\\\n## Why the remaining support should be preserved\\\\n\\\\nThe other eight generated test cases passed in the native executable. They continue to provide valid coverage for checksum initialization, class resolution, Java serialization codecs, object stream handling, and protobuf nano construction without depending on the unsupported shared-arena cleaner path. Removing those tests would discard working, consumer-relevant support unrelated to this failure.\\\",\\n./docs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:23:| **Repository automation (Forge)** | Generate or repair metadata using LLM-driven pipelines. | Per coordinate, the toolkit can: (1) **add support for a new library** — generate a JUnit / Kotlin / Scala test suite, scaffold metadata, and iterate until JVM-mode tests pass and dynamic-access is collected ([`add_new_library_support.py`](../../forge/ai_workflows/drivers/add_new_library_support.py)); (2) **fix a Java compilation (`javac`) failure** raised by a library version bump ([`fix_javac_fail.py`](../../forge/ai_workflows/drivers/fix_javac_fail.py)); (3) **fix a JVM-mode (`javaTest`) runtime failure** raised by a version bump ([`fix_java_run_fail.py`](../../forge/ai_workflows/drivers/fix_java_run_fail.py)); (4) **fix a `native-image` runtime failure** raised by a version bump ([`fix_ni_run.py`](../../forge/ai_workflows/drivers/fix_ni_run.py)); (5) **improve dynamic-access coverage** of already-supported libraries by targeting uncovered call sites; (6) **post-generation repair** of the metadata produced by a previous run ([`post_generation_fix.py`](../../forge/ai_workflows/core/post_generation_fix.py), [`metadata_fix.py`](../../forge/ai_workflows/core/metadata_fix.py)). Each task runs Gradle tasks against a worktree of this repo, appends a schema-validated metrics record, and — when invoked through [`forge/git_scripts/publish_*.py`](../../forge/git_scripts/) — pushes a verified branch that trusted GitHub Actions turn into a PR for human review. See [forge/docs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md](../../forge/docs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md). |\\n./tests/tck-test-support/src/main/java/org/graalvm/internal/tck/FullStackTraceTestExecutionListener.java:19:/// which forces the metadata-fix tooling to rediscover it from scratch.\\n./tests/src/org.springframework.integration/spring-integration-sftp/7.1.1/gradle.properties:4:library.coordinates = org.springframework.integration:spring-integration-sftp:7.1.1\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\nh